## Methodology
The project was developed using the Pima Indians Diabetes Dataset. The dataset was preprocessed by handling missing values, scaling numerical features, and preparing the data for model training.
Two ensemble machine learning algorithms, **Random Forest** and **XGBoost**, were selected because they provide high accuracy, handle complex relationships between features effectively, reduce overfitting, and perform well on healthcare datasets.
The dataset was divided into training and testing sets. Models were trained on the training data and evaluated on unseen test data using performance metrics such as Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-Score.
## Results
- Accuracy: **97%**
- Recall: **92%**

The results demonstrate the effectiveness of ensemble learning techniques for diabetes risk prediction and healthcare analytics.
